{"id":655,"slug":"the-hidden-fortress","title":"The Hidden Fortress","year":1958,"country":"Japan","duration":139,"spine":116,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/655-the-hidden-fortress","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/58e97ae4dd0b361bd131525faf284b78/K10x3FugjRS01iYKEXsLTr0OlDQk4P_large.jpg","description":"A grand-scale adventure as only Akira Kurosawa could make one, The Hidden Fortress stars the inimitable Toshiro Mifune as a general charged with guarding his defeated clan’s princess (a fierce Misa Uehara) as the two smuggle royal treasure across hostile territory. Accompanying them are a pair of bumbling, conniving peasants who may or may not be their friends. This rip-roaring ride is among the director’s most beloved films and was a primary influence on George Lucas’s Star Wars. The Hidden Fortress delivers Kurosawa’s trademark deft blend of wry humor, breathtaking action, and compassionate humanity.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Akira Kurosawa","slug":"akira-kurosawa"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Toshiro Mifune","role":"General Rokurota Makabe","slug":"toshiro-mifune"},{"actor":"Minoru Chiaki","role":"Tahei","slug":"minoru-chiaki"},{"actor":"Kamatari Fujiwara","role":"Matashichi","slug":"kamatari-fujiwara"},{"actor":"Susumu Fujita","role":"Hyoe Tadokoro","slug":"susumu-fujita"},{"actor":"Misa Uehara","role":"Princess Yuki","slug":"misa-uehara"},{"actor":"Takashi Shimura","role":"Izumi Nagakura","slug":"takashi-shimura"},{"actor":"Eiko Miyoshi","role":"Lady-in-waiting","slug":"eiko-miyoshi"},{"actor":"Toshiko Higuchi","role":"Slave girl","slug":"toshiko-higuchi"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Akira Kurosawa","slug":"akira-kurosawa"},{"role":"Executive producers","person":"Sanezumi Fujimoto","slug":null},{"role":"Executive producers","person":"Akira Kurosawa","slug":"akira-kurosawa"},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Ryuzo Kikushima","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Hideo Oguni","slug":null},{"role":"Scre